From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] stall guard: a short reply ending on ':' with zero
 tool calls re-prompts

A reply like 'Reading the card first, together with the PR:' announced its next
step and stopped (defect agent-b6540f8eef); trailing_continue_intent() only knew
'let me now / I'll now / next, I'. trailing_colon_handoff() treats a <=400-char
prose reply whose last character is ':' (not inside an open code fence) as a stall
when tools are offered and the turn made no tool calls. Same bounded counter (max
2 re-prompts) and the same 'Stall guard: turn ending on trailing continue-intent'
log line.
